			"date": "2024-04-30T13:50:55.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@Chris\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>Chris</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@dries\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>dries</span></a></span> It’s incredibly easy to underestimate the amount of time and energy that’s gone into the Views/FieldAPI/Entity system over the past *checks watch* NINETEEN YEARS. Starting fresh gives orgs that need a small subset of that a lot more agility from a code perspective, but it’s easy to compile a “critical feature list” that takes 2x as long to build and just as much to maintain…</p>",
